},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"printing difficulty. Thus a treble clef line noted with 8va will be indicated with an octave-shift down from","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"the pitch data indicated in the notes. A size of 8 indicates one octave; a size of 15 indicates two octaves.","type":"text"}],"url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxloctaveshift","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLOctaveShift","type":"topic","role":"symbol","kind":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"text":"MXLOctaveShift","kind":"identifier"}],"title":"MXLOctaveShift","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"MXLOctaveShift","kind":"identifier"}]},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLDirection/Kind-swift.struct/Content-swift.enum":{"role":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxldirection\/kind-swift.struct\/content-swift.enum","type":"topic","fragments":[{"text":"enum","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Content","kind":"identifier"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"text":"Content","kind":"identifier"}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"One of the alternatives for DirectionType."}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLDirection\/Kind-swift.struct\/Content-swift.enum","title":"MXLDirection.Kind.Content","kind":"symbol"},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLDirection":{"role":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxldirection","type":"topic","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"MXLDirection","kind":"identifier"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"text":"MXLDirection","kind":"identifier"}],"abstract":[{"text":"A direction is a musical indication that is not necessarily attached to a specific note. Two or more may be","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"combined to indicate words followed by the start of a dashed line, the end of a wedge followed by dynamics,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":"etc. For applications where a specific direction is indeed attached to a specific note, the direction element"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":"can be associated with the first note element that follows it in score order that is not in a different voice."}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLDirection","title":"MXLDirection","kind":"symbol"},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL":{"url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl","kind":"symbol","type":"topic","role":"collection","title":"IvorMXL","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A MusicXML parser, normalizer, validator, and formatter."}]},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLDirection/Kind-swift.struct/Content-swift.enum/octaveShift(_:)":{"abstract":[{"text":"An octave shift indicating notes shifted up or down from their true pitched values.","type":"text"}],"url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxldirection\/kind-swift.struct\/content-swift.enum\/octaveshift(_:)","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLDirection\/Kind-swift.struct\/Content-swift.enum\/octaveShift(_:)","type":"topic","role":"symbol","kind":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"case","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"octaveShift","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"(","kind":"text"},{"text":"MXLOctaveShift","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:7IvorMXL14MXLOctaveShiftV"},{"text":")","kind":"text"}],"title":"MXLDirection.Kind.Content.octaveShift(_:)"},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLDirection/Kind-swift.struct":{"role":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxldirection\/kind-swift.struct","type":"topic","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Kind","kind":"identifier"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"text":"Kind","kind":"identifier"}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Textual direction types may have more than 1 component due to multiple fonts. The dynamics element may also be"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"used in the notations element. Attribute groups related to print suggestions apply to the individual"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"direction-type, not to the overall direction."}],"title":"MXLDirection.Kind","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLDirection\/Kind-swift.struct","kind":"symbol"}}}